# The stock vendor policy labels the fan control nodes in vendor_file_contexts
# (/sys/kernel/fan -> sysfs_nb_fan). Sysfs nodes only get file_contexts labels
# through restorecon, so apply them once the driver has created the nodes.
#
# The stock init.qcom.rc makes the nodes system 0664, and the stock system wrote
# them from system_server. GrimoNX809JCooling runs under its own UID instead, so
# the two nodes it writes are opened up the way the stock init.vendor.rc does for
# the pump. The chmod runs as init, which needs the setattr rule in
# sepolicy/system_ext/private; the same file lets the app's writes cross MLS
# levels. SELinux still limits writers to the domains the stock vendor policy
# names, platform_app among them.
on boot
    restorecon /sys/kernel/fan
    restorecon /sys/kernel/fan/fan_enable
    restorecon /sys/kernel/fan/fan_speed_count
    restorecon /sys/kernel/fan/fan_speed_level
    chmod 0666 /sys/kernel/fan/fan_enable
    chmod 0666 /sys/kernel/fan/fan_speed_level
